  "changelog": "v177: fix(163): structured close \u2014 {takeaway_prose, hook}, render only the prose (ADR 0014). Issue #163: a conversation close leaked model scaffolding into the user's bubble \u2014 eval commentary on the owner's conversational behavior, a continuity instruction addressed to the next session's model, and the hook rendered as a labeled field with raw markdown. The closing generation contract (conversation_delivery._closing_output_contract(), appended after conversation.build_closing_prompt()) now asks for exactly one JSON object, {\"takeaway_prose\": str, \"hook\": str|null}; the new parse_closing_output() (alongside the existing parse_turn_output(), same _valid_message structural-sanity authority) parses it with NO raw-text fallback \u2014 a close that isn't valid structured JSON is unconditionally malformed_generation, the same silent-degradation path every other closing failure already used (the pre-#163 fallback that let scaffolding-in-message-text through is deleted, not narrowed). _deliver_closing() renders ONLY takeaway_prose and returns hook separately; close_session_now() persists it additively on the session's close block (close.hook) only alongside an actually-delivered takeaway; _write_outcome() ledgers hook so a replayed already-confirmed close reconstructs it. Four new closing-only lint classes in conversation_lints.lint_closing_phrases() (data in evals/lints.yaml, engine stays generic): closing_label_leak (literal labeled-field substrings \u2014 \"Hook for next time:\", \"Takeaway:\", \"For next time:\"), closing_meta_commentary (case-insensitive regex judging the conversation's own quality or the author's conversational behavior, distinct from rule 8's allowed appreciation of what was shared), closing_future_turn (a clause-initial \"next time,\" + imperative shape \u2014 engine constant _FUTURE_TURN_CLAUSE_RE, same precedent as _PRESUPPOSING_RE \u2014 plus literal future-turn phrases), and closing_markdown_leak (raw ** emphasis). behavior.md rule 8 gains a new paragraph naming all four bans (rule numbers unchanged, per file's own load-bearing-numbering rule); the handbook's byte-exact embed (docs/handbook/interactions/conversation.md) moved in the same commit, verified via tests/test_handbook_parity.py's EmbedParityTests. turn-instructions.md's closing bullet and conversation.py's build_closing_prompt() checklist both describe the woven, never-labeled shape (the exact JSON mechanics stay in the appended output-contract text, same split as every other builder). Two new goldens: chat-porch-swing-closing.json (a new synthetic PASS example, swept normally \u2014 the two pre-existing closing goldens already pass the new checks unmodified) and closing-scaffold-leak-bad-01.json (a deliberately-broken, entirely synthetic fixture reproducing issue #163's leaked SHAPE, excluded from interaction_evals.load_goldens()'s sweep via a NON_GOLDEN_FILENAMES entry \u2014 same mechanism the router fixture files already use \u2014 since tests/test_structured_close.py loads it directly to prove all four lints trip). New tests/test_structured_close.py (30 tests) plus fixture-shape updates in tests/test_conversation_delivery.py and tests/test_conversation_router.py where they pinned the pre-#163 free-text/{\"message\": ...} closing shape. ADR 0014 also records (not implements) the platform pin-bump rider: the hosted close path parses the same structure and Firestore's CloseInfo gains hook additively. conversation-evals keyless layers green (6/6 goldens); full suite zero delta vs. the pre-existing 21-failure baseline.",
